{"name":"Paradise Island","hex":"#5aa7a0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Paradise Island","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An island of the Bahamas."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Paradise_Island"}],"entries":[{"title":"Paradise Island","blocks":[{"text":"Paradise Island is an island in the Bahamas formerly known as Hog Island. The island, with an area of 277 hectares, is just off the shore of the city of Nassau, which is itself on the northern edge of the island of New Providence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Paradise_Island_Lighthouse%2C_Bahamas.jpg/330px-Paradise_Island_Lighthouse%2C_Bahamas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise_Island","wikidata":"Q3181503"},{"title":"Paradise Island (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Paradise Island is the third studio album by Lake, released in 1979."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Lake_Paradise_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise_Island_(album)","wikidata":"Q7134296"},{"title":"Paradise","blocks":[{"text":"In religion and folklore, paradise is a place of everlasting happiness, delight, and bliss. Paradisiacal notions are often laden with pastoral imagery, and may be cosmogonical, eschatological, or both, often contrasted with the miseries of human civilization: in paradise there is only peace, prosperity, and happiness. Paradise is a place of contentment, a land of luxury and fulfillment containing ever-lasting bliss and delight. Paradise is often described as a \"higher place\", the holiest place, in contrast to this world, or underworlds such as hell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Angelico%2C_giudizio_universale_01.jpg/330px-Angelico%2C_giudizio_universale_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradise","wikidata":"Q3363340"},{"title":"Island","blocks":[{"text":"An island or isle is a piece of land, distinct from a continent, completely surrounded by water. There are continental islands, which were formed by being split from a continent by plate tectonics, and oceanic islands, which have never been part of a continent. Oceanic islands can be formed from volcanic activity, grow into atolls from coral reefs, and form from sediment along shorelines, creating barrier islands. River islands can also form from sediment and debris in rivers. Artificial islands are those made by humans, including small rocky outcroppings built out of lagoons and large-scale land reclamation projects used for development."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg/330px-Hawaje-NoRedLine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Island","wikidata":"Q23442"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Atlantis_Paradise_Island_Hotel_edit.jpg/500px-Atlantis_Paradise_Island_Hotel_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Atlantis_Paradise_Island_Hotel_edit.jpg/960px-Atlantis_Paradise_Island_Hotel_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Atlantis_Paradise_Island_Hotel_edit.jpg/500px-Atlantis_Paradise_Island_Hotel_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAtlantis_Paradise_Island_Hotel_edit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Frenchcloisters.jpg/330px-Frenchcloisters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t